getnameinfo printed "ipv6 is not fully supported in this function" to
standard error for every IPv6 address, so nc and ssh said it on each
IPv6 connection, and it dropped a link-local address's scope, so
fe80::1 came back without the link it is on. It now says nothing, and
names a scoped address's scope after a %, as glibc does: a link-local
or link-local multicast address's interface by name (fe80::1%net0), or
by number with NI_NUMERICSCOPE, when the interface is gone, or for
another scope (ADR 0341).
Meant for upstream.

